Source: ipu7-ov05c10-camera
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: corentin-core <110186540+corentin-core@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/corentin-core/ipu7-ov05c10-camera

Package: ipu7-ov05c10-camera-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Description: kernel drivers for OV05C10 cameras behind an Intel IPU7
 Three drivers Ubuntu does not ship, needed to make the built-in camera of
 Intel Lunar Lake laptops work: the OV05C10 sensor, the Intel CVS bridge that
 arbitrates the CSI-2 link, and a replacement ipu-bridge that knows about it.
 .
 Two of them carry local patches. See
 /usr/src/ipu7-ov05c10-camera-${binary:Version}/PROVENANCE.md.

Package: ipu7-camera-ondemand
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         v4l-utils,
         gstreamer1.0-tools,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
# Versioned so it is only pulled where the distribution ships a libcamera new
# enough for the IPU7. On older releases apt skips it, which is what we want:
# the 0.2 plugin would clash with a libcamera built under /usr/local.
Recommends: ipu7-ov05c10-camera-dkms,
            gstreamer1.0-libcamera (>= 0.6)
Description: on-demand virtual webcam fed by an IPU7 camera
 Exposes the camera as a plain V4L2 device, /dev/video42, that browsers and
 conferencing apps accept. The sensor is powered up only while an application
 has the device open, and powered down again a few seconds after it closes.
 .
 Needs libcamera 0.6 or later with software ISP support: Ubuntu 26.04 and
 later ship it, earlier releases need a build from source.
 .
 Also needs a v4l2loopback that builds against your kernel. Ubuntu's 0.12.7
 does not build on 7.0, so it is deliberately not a dependency; see the
 README for the upstream version.
